  "title": "learnwithmrcedric: Computing and the Spreadsheet Coaches",
  "notes": [
    "New portal (page release 31, nothing to paste): a glass sign-in card over a live night sky with a black hole, stars and drifting equations",
    "Mark by page (page release 30, nothing to paste): in the checking screen, By page marks one page at a time across the whole class, saving each script in the background as you go",
    "Palm guard (page release 29, nothing to paste): once an iPad has used an Apple Pencil, a resting palm no longer writes on worksheets or drops ticks on the checking screen, and a Pencil that lands while a palm is down takes over",
    "Computing: a Computing door on the portal opens the students' Computing page (class tiles, name, PIN keypad), with the Spreadsheet Coaches open to their class and every Excel file they have checked",
    "Computing students are listed in their own tab, Computing students, in the Teacher Hub sheet, and have their own PINs, apart from Science",
    "Each file a Coach checks is saved to Drive (Worksheet Hub > Computing > class > sub-chapter > student code), every try kept, named by code, never by name",
    "The Teacher Hub's new Computing tab: open each Coach to a class, the grid of newest tries with Drive links, Reset PIN, and which Coach files are in Drive",
    "The Coaches and task files stay private in Drive (Worksheet Hub > Computing > Coaches and task files)",
    "Paste or install: App.gs (changed) and ComputingCode.gs (new). The pages update themselves"
  ],
